Execution

When the developer submits the program:

* Rust receives the exact source;
* the Vector Language compiler parses it;
* the AST is validated;
* symbols and references are resolved;
* types and permissions are checked;
* the kernel verifies the requested hierarchy;
* creation operations require the relevant authorization and validator scope;
* transfer requests enforce the Token-only dimension rule;
* required validators independently verify the proposal;
* the operation enters consensus;
* commitment occurs atomically;
* event history and resulting state roots are recorded;
* the developer receives a verifiable execution report.

Failed execution

